# <%= it.title %> MCP server

<% if (it.libraries) { %>
MCP server for the libraries of **<%= it.title.replace(/ libraries$/, "") %>**, each in the version the project uses, generated by
[make-mcp](https://github.com/make-mcp/make-mcp) on <%= it.generatedAt %>.

| Library | Version | Pages | Releases | Signatures | License | Documentation |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
<% for (const l of it.libraries) { %>| <%= l.title %> (`<%= l.name %>`) | <%= l.version %> | <%= l.pageCount %> | <%= l.changeCount || "–" %> | <%= l.symbolCount || "–" %> | <%= l.license || "unknown" %> | <%= l.contentMode === "embedded" ? "embedded" : "downloaded on install" %> |
<% } %>
<% } else { %>
MCP server for **<%= it.title %> <%= it.version %>**, generated by [make-mcp](https://github.com/make-mcp/make-mcp) on <%= it.generatedAt %>.
<% } %>

<% if (it.docs) { %>
## Documentation tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `search_docs` | Full-text search across <%= it.docs.pageCount %> pages |
| `get_page` | Full Markdown of a page |
| `list_topics` | All pages grouped by section |
<% if (it.docs.componentCount) { %>| `get_component` | One of <%= it.docs.componentCount %> components with class names and examples |
<% } %>
<% if (it.docs.changeCount) { %>| `changes_since` | Release notes after a version (<%= it.docs.changeCount %> releases) – what changed, for upgrades |
<% } %>
<% if (it.docs.symbolCount) { %>| `get_signature` | Exact signatures of <%= it.docs.symbolCount %> exported functions, classes and types, read from the installed package |
<% } %>

Every page is also available as resource `docs://<%= it.name %>/{path}`.
<% if (it.libraries) { %>
The tools take an optional `library` (the name in brackets above); without it they search all libraries.

The documentation of permissively licensed libraries is embedded under `data/corpus/` with attribution to its
authors. Libraries under other or unknown licenses are downloaded from their original source on your machine
(`npm run refresh` / `uv run server.py --refresh`) and cached under `~/.cache/make-mcp/`. Do not redistribute the cache.
<% } else { %>

**Source:** <% for (const s of it.docs.sources) { %><%= s.url %><% if (s.ref) { %> @ <%= s.ref %><% } %> <% } %>  
**License of the documentation:** <%= it.license || "unknown" %>.
<% if (it.docs.contentMode === "embedded") { %>
The documentation is embedded under `data/corpus.json` with attribution to its authors as permitted by its license.
<% } else { %>
The documentation is **not** included in this package. It is downloaded from the original source on your machine
(`npm run refresh` / `uv run server.py --refresh`) and cached under `~/.cache/make-mcp/`. Do not redistribute the cache.
<% } %>
<% } %>
<% } %>
<% if (it.api) { %>
## API tools

<% if (it.api.extracted) { %>
> The operations were extracted from the prose documentation by an LLM. Each one was checked against the page
> it was quoted from, but parameters and bodies can still be incomplete – review `data/api.json` before relying on it.
<% } %>
<% if (it.api.toolMode === "grouped") { %>
<%= it.api.endpointCount %> operations of **<%= it.api.title %>** (`<%= it.api.baseUrl %>`), exposed through three tools so the
agent's context stays small:

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `list_operations` | Find operations by tag or keyword |
| `describe_operation` | Parameters and request body of one operation |
| `call_operation` | Call an operation with arguments |
<% } else { %>
<%= it.api.endpointCount %> operations of **<%= it.api.title %>** (`<%= it.api.baseUrl %>`), one tool per operation.
<% } %>
Side-effect-free GET operations are additionally exposed as resources (`api://<%= it.name %>/…`).

### Configuration

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
<% for (const v of it.envVars) { %>| `<%= v.name %>` | <%= v.description %> |
<% } %>
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` or pass the variables via your MCP client configuration.
<% } %>
